A||||14||SLAMMED87GT||Celica......."Looks Fast"||||1||
Z||000000||SLAMMED87GT||12-30-2001||01:54 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Celica.jpg"> <P>Notice the caption- "Looks Fast". Just goes to show you that it's not like it's only the cheap aftermarktet company's supplying the "ricers" with products that only enhance their Civic or Accord. <P>This is how certain manufacturers market their cars now as seen above. That Celica isn't that fast but it has the looks! That is enough to attract a huge young demographic that is looking for just that. A fast looking car. You can get aftermarket parts for a Celica to make it faster, but the idea is: market a car by it's looks- this approach can make companies a lot of money. Honda is doing the same thing, just less apparent. They are offering "styling accessories for the Civic as seen on a recent magazine ad.<P>Just a simple observation.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||12-30-2001||03:33 PM||||That's just it. The "muscle-car" tuning crowd has shifted it's focus AWAY from performance, and more towards "Looks"<P>Truth be known, that is the reason I hold "ricers" in contempt. There is VERY little out there that truly gives those cars any measure of "performance." 140HP after a turbo/supercharger? Whoop-de-friggen-do. 0-60 in under 7s? Come talk to me when you hit the 5s.<P>Clear tail lights, shoulder pads, fake roll-cages, racing buckets on STREET cars... Ask them to race? you either spank them harshly, lose because you have an even slower car, or they tell you "it's a show car." <P>Super spoilers... Ground-FX. Ugly as sin, yes. Reason for contempt? Not really. But when you drive the thing like it's the hottest ****  on the road, don't even talk to me. Show me wind-tunnel tests that prove that your add-ons do more than just add weight? Oh, you can't? You bought them because they LOOK aero-dynamic? <P>I don't like the trend in auto-enthusiasm. The emphasis is on numbers, and looks, rather than actual performance. 5hp muffler, 10hp ignition, 5 hp headers, 5hp intake, 5hp filter... 30 extra HP? Uh, RIGHT. By that logic, every fool with $100 invested in parts would be running full SECONDS faster on their slips... Pull the other one, it's got bells on.<P>Still, you can't fault the auto-makers. The young'uns WANT the look. To get REAL performance with appropriate fuel-economy, you need to spend BIG. It's not like the 60s and 70s where you could piss away at 10mpg, and compensate for low-efficiency motors with sheer displacement. So as opposed to raising the car's price (and performance), all they really have to do is be a little more shaky when drawing the lines of the car, and imitating the common bolt-ons, such as exhaust tips. The auto-makers aren't propagating the phenomenon, they are listening to the buyer. ||||reg||7
Z||000002||Joe Torma||12-30-2001||06:58 PM||||Well said Mach10.<P>You notice they only can claim it "looks fast"?!<BR>If they said it was fast...false advertising!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||12-30-2001||09:40 PM||||I'll second the "well said" for Mach10.<P>I know they are marketed at young buyers, but how many of their 18-24 target audience can really afford them.  I saw one of those Celica GTS's at a local Toyota dealer with the fast looking fx like seen in the pic.  Now the GTS sticker was already $24,500 some odd dollars.  I believe the package price that was stuck next to the sticker was $1899.  Now thats almost $26.5K for a car that only LOOKS fast.  I dunno many teens/young adults that can really afford this car, unless mommy and daddy are buying (happens a lot too!).<P>Maybe this is the reason... when junior wants a car and mommy is worried about "dangerous" fast cars and daddy is concerned with insurance premiums these fast looking slugs get bought.  Otherwise, you can get a 'Stang GT that'll do 5's out of the box and blow all your buddies in their 4-banger ricers into the weeds! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||12-31-2001||01:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>I'll second the "well said" for Mach10.<P>I know they are marketed at young buyers, but how many of their 18-24 target audience can really afford them.  I saw one of those Celica GTS's at a local Toyota dealer with the fast looking fx like seen in the pic.  Now the GTS sticker was already $24,500 some odd dollars.  I believe the package price that was stuck next to the sticker was $1899.  Now thats almost $26.5K for a car that only LOOKS fast.  I dunno many teens/young adults that can really afford this car, unless mommy and daddy are buying (happens a lot too!).<P>Maybe this is the reason... when junior wants a car and mommy is worried about "dangerous" fast cars and daddy is concerned with insurance premiums these fast looking slugs get bought.  Otherwise, you can get a 'Stang GT that'll do 5's out of the box and blow all your buddies in their 4-banger ricers into the weeds! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't know how slutty the dealerships and financers are down in the states, but up here, they will put out for ANY customer. Failing that, a parental co-sign isn't too hard for most people. I swear, 95% of the (newer) cars driven by youngsters on our streets aren't actually OWNED by the driver... A co-sign will go a LONG way... ||||reg||7
Z||000005||artherd||12-31-2001||01:19 AM||||180bhp out of a NA 1.8L motor isn't bad (it just needs only about twice that displacement, and cylinders  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   and a 6-speed stick shift all for $20grand dosen't really suck...<P>Come on you guys, we're living in the days of THE FASTEST street legal production cars EVER.  BMW's M5 will clock a 4.8sec 0.60 time.  The M3 matches that time.   The vette/911/F360 are the fastest they ever been.<P>All this with a bunch of power-everything, airbags in the trunk, and a decent quality sound system with a comfortable cabin in which to enjoy it all.<P>The 60s sucked for automotive performance (they did have style!)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR>Just playing a little devil's advocate  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000006||NOCONES||12-31-2001||01:23 AM||||um.. don't those have a 180 hp VVTLI engine, with a six speed manual tranny.  i think 0-60 comes up it a  lil under 6 seconds.. i don't know what book you guys go by, but that is fast.  And come on, it's the looks that sell any car.  YOU drive a car everyday that was succesfull because of it's looks.  YOUR car too has 140 hp, and does 0-60 in 7s.  The fiero was sold, and survived because of it's looks.  Sure it's a blast to drive, but so are those new celica's.  Laugh at them all you want, but most "ricers" out there have cars that could take a fiero 0-60. We just have to worry about if any of them can learn how to drive.||||reg||1
Z||000007||GTFiero1||12-31-2001||01:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B><P>The 60s sucked for automotive performance (they did have style!)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>man 60's were all about performance. the 64 was the first muscle car, the GTO. my brother has a 68 GTO and even when he's just lightly accelerating you can feel the torque. you dont feel crap in my dad's friend's new Mustang GT<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
